{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>זובח</b> Two times in the Masorah: זובח לאלקים, זובח תודה יכבדנני. One who slaughters and gives thanks to HaKadosh Barukh Hu, honors Him and sees Him in the salvation of Elohim. But one who slaughters to elohim (other gods) — יחרם." "<b>יחרם</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and the others: יחרם מן האדם לא יפדה, יחרם כל רכושו. זובח לאלהים יחרם כל רכושו — and that is what they said: one who engages in commerce at a fair of idolaters, the animal is removed and has no redemption, as it is written יחרם לא יפדה — it seizes its monetary value."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:04.695593780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}